Unclosed title tag causes JSoup to "eat up" rest of document


<p dir="auto">Hi:</p>
<p dir="auto">We've come across an issue with parsing a document with an unclosed title tag. JSoup<br/>
seems to "eat up" the rest of the document in its parsing and thus no elements after<br/>
the unclosed tag are available after the parse.</p>
<p dir="auto">While this is obviously not a valid document Firefox seems to handle it OK by displaying<br/>
the document and saying "Untitled document" in its title bar.</p>
<p dir="auto">We come across a lot of badly formed documents in our web crawls so having a fix<br/>
for this issue would be much appreciated. I've given some sample source below<br/>
which demonstrates the bug (tested against JSoup 1.5.2).</p>
<p dir="auto">Many thanks,</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Francis.</li>
</ul>
